.TITLE "sort"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Sorts lines of text in files or piped data. It can arrange data __alphabetically__, __numerically__, or in __reverse order__, making it easier to analyze large lists.

.DIV "TLDR"
**sort file**
Sorts the lines of a file alphabetically and displays the result.
> __file__ the target file

**sort -r file**
Sorts the lines in reverse (descending) order.
> __-r__ reverse flag | __file__ the target file

**sort -n file**
Sorts the lines numerically instead of alphabetically.
> __-n__ numeric sort flag | __file__ the target file

**sort -u file**
Sorts the lines and removes any duplicate entries from the output.
> __-u__ unique flag | __file__ the target file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Combining __sort__ with __uniq__ is a powerful way to process data logs. For files with multiple columns, you can use the __-k__ flag to specify which column should be used as the primary sorting key.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:uniq** **linux:grep**

documentation: __https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/sort__
